{"title":"1986 AJHSME Problems/Problem 22","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Alan, Beth, Carlos, and Diana were discussing their possible grades in mathematics class this grading period.  Alan said, \"If I get an A, then Beth will get an A.\"  Beth said, \"If I get an A, then Carlos will get an A.\"  Carlos said, \"If I get an A, then Diana will get an A.\"  All of these statements were true, but only two of the students received an A.  Which two received A's?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/2/5c2f2209919300b6801589711ecf5a636ab3085a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(A)}\\ \\text{Alan, Beth} \\qquad \\text{(B)}\\ \\text{Beth, Carlos} \\qquad \\text{(C)}\\ \\text{Carlos, Diana}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"428\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/9/f896e7b710ed06424a4e0e267755a086e6face63.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(D)}\\ \\text{Alan, Diana} \\qquad \\text{(E)}\\ \\text{Beth, Diana}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"270\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If Alan got an A, then Beth, and therefore Carlos and Diana would also get A's.  But only two students actually got A's, so Alan did not get an A.\n</p><p>If Beth got an A, then Carlos, and therefore Diana would get also get A's.  Once again, this is impossible since only two students got A's.  Therefore, Beth did not get an A.\n</p><p>By process of elimination, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/d/ccdb9164a5ac15f6958cff5b1aeb3a4ab2b074e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(C)}\\ \\text{Carlos, Diana}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"147\" height=\"30\" /> must have gotten A's.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_AJHSME\" title=\"1986 AJHSME\">1986 AJHSME</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_AJHSME_Problems\" title=\"1986 AJHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_AJHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1986 AJHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=42&amp;year=1986\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"1986 AJHSME Problems/Problem 21\">Problem 21</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"1986 AJHSME Problems/Problem 23\">Problem 23</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1986 AJHSME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a